WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.690
I was starting to wonder if you'd 
arrive before I became an old granny.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.740
You're Otto's helper?

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.620
Calling me a "helper" makes 
it sound as if we're equals.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:12.030
I am an attendant.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:14.580
You're talking like you're a 
witch's familiar or something...

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.220
My orders from Roswaal-sama 
were to assist you.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.810
It was my own decision to seek 
out Otto to meet that end.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:24.830
So he measured up to your standards?

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.200
I just thought if there was 
no one I could handily use,

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.550
you would end up dying in vain.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.460
Crap! I can't deny that!

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.650
Well, you should!

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.220
For someone who's been confined, 
you seem awfully composed.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.800
Well, I did just have a good laugh.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.080
We're going to escape.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.390
Garf can't leave the graveyard

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.480
while Emilia-sama is attempting the trial.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.620
We'll leave while his 
attention is away from us.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:53.340
No.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:55.880
Running away can wait until later.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.010
Natsuki-san?

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.620
I'm not saying we won't run,

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.110
but this is a golden opportunity.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.330
What are you planning?

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.970
I'm going to do what I was trying to do 
three days ago, before I was interrupted.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:16.900
<b>If it's</b>

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:18.950
<b>to save you</b>

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:20.160
<b>I don't care</b>

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:21.660
<b>how many times</b>

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:24.330
<b>I die</b>

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.470
Roswaal,

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:43.470
I won't let you hide 
anything from me this time.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.610
Reunited after three days...

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:48.730
It doesn't quite feel 
like a miraculous return.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.280
Quit joking around.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.560
I don't have time to put up 
with your dumb games right now.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.110
It was Ram who let you in, yes?

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:59.400
I did order her to help you.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.750
Yeah. That's why she let me 
in here without argument.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.790
I put the idea of running away on hold.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.250
Oh?

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:13.200
I want to ask you something under the assumption
 that my leaving the Sanctuary is a given.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.100
Of course. If I have the answer,
 I will give it to you.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.210
If anything, it's something 
<i>only</i> you can answer.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:26.320
Is Beatrice... a member of the Witch's Cult?

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:33.330
What made you suspect that Beatrice 
may be a witch cultist?

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.640
I saw her in the forbidden library.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.590
She had a Gospel.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.660
If she is a witch cultist...

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.620
That makes her our...

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.420
<i>My</i> enemy.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:52.070
Those are strong words.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.830
Words that took true resolve to say.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.380
And...

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.650
Even if you say them with 
such a pained expression,

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.800
they are not very convincing.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:08.270
The idea that you and she should 
become enemies is truly awful.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:12.520
So I would like to offer you a helping hand.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:15.450
You, offer me a helping hand?

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.960
That's gotta be one of the 
shadiest statements ever.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:22.530
It is true that what you saw was 
something closely resembling a Gospel.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.220
It makes sense that you 
would suspect it to be one.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.270
But you have my word

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.700
that she is not a witch cultist.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:32.330
You mean that?!

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:36.360
That book of hers is not a Gospel.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.780
It is a magical text that 
tells the true future,

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.090
of which only two copies exist in the world.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:44.590
It is the closest there 
is to the Tome of Wisdom.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.520
Tome of Wisdom?

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.350
But she definitely said it was a Gospel!

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:54.640
Everything I do is in accordance with 
the Gospel's guidance, I suppose!

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.640
That is because it lacks an official name.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:00.680
Thus, it is given the same name 
used for the defective versions.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:01.950
Defective?

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:08.190
Well, as long as she's not a 
witch cultist, it's fine.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:12.160
The question is, how can I get her to help me?

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.960
"Roswaal said you are to ask the question."

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:17.580
Huh?

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:22.070
If you say this to Beatrice, 
she should respond.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.300
You mean...

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.180
"Roswaal said to ask the question."

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.660
I see.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.480
It appears these words are insufficient for you.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.990
H-Hang on... Insufficient?

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.560
Then tell her this:

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:42.470
"I am that person."

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:44.090
That person?

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:46.320
Get Beatrice to ask the question,

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.530
then answer it affirmatively.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.860
If you do that,

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:54.560
she will, without a doubt, ally with you.

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:58.090
How can you be so sure?

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:02.960
Because it is in the contract that 
she is powerless to override.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.920
Contract...

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:12.280
If this doesn't work, I'll punch
 you right in the face!

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:15.020
That I can promise you, no matter what you say!

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:19.560
Very well. Do as you please.

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:22.160
Once you have allied with Beatrice,

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:27.540
she will surely be a great help in solving 
all the problems concerning the Sanctuary.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:32.160
Roswaal, I have one last question.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.030
What is it?

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:39.040
You're not actually our enemy, are you?

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:41.670
Of course not.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:44.000
I am an ally to all of you.

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:48.510
Did you get any answers?

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.950
Yeah, quite a few.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:52.140
I think all the pieces fit together now.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.400
What's the plan?

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.220
A carriage would be too conspicuous.

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:57.730
You and I will have to ride together.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:06:59.090
Is that all right?

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.530
I guess you'd be in danger 
if you stayed here, too.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:02.590
I have no prob—

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:04.020
Oh, wait!

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:07.870
Once we're out of the Sanctuary, 
our first stop is the mansion.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:11.050
We can't just leave Frederica 
to fend for herself.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:13.230
But if it's just us two...

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.530
That's hardly enough to fight if need be.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.870
In other words, you want me to go with you?

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:23.460
Well, if you would... I mean... 
I'd feel a lot better.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.600
I suppose I must.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.760
You're sure?

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:34.760
Roswaal-sama did order me 
to help you, after all.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:35.560
But...

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.490
How will we travel?

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:40.360
There's only one ground dragon and three of us.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:41.220
Oh...

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.320
Even if both of you only amount to half a man,

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.310
you each take up enough space for a full man.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.930
I don't think three of us 
will fit on one dragon.

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:51.080
Was the "half a man" comment necessary?!

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.740
Havin' a cozy little chat 
while ya take a walk?

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:57.900
Well, since I'm here, why not
 let me in on the fun?

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:06.040
The brighter it shines, the farther 
away the magrizza goes, as they say!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.660
Shouldn't you be overseeing 
the trial right now?

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:11.060
Do you have time to waste 
hanging around here?!

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:14.850
My job is to protect this Sanctuary!

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:18.640
So if the Sanctuary's under threat, 
you better believe I have time!

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:22.840
You couldn't escape the eyes of this Sanctuary!

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:24.520
Eyes of the Sanctuary?

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.230
I'm just sayin' your little plans were leaked.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:30.150
So? Where d'ya think you're headin' off to?

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:31.780
Well?!

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:35.730
We're going to get Barusu 
outside the Sanctuary.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:39.540
He'll cause trouble for 
you if he stays here, too,

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:41.980
so I'd say this works out perfectly for you.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:44.640
Think you know what's goin' 
on in my head, do ya?

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:46.720
Damn, there ain't nothin' 
lovable about you at all.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:48.560
That's what I like about ya, though.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:53.300
So can we assume that you're 
agreeing to let us go?

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:54.840
What?!

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:59.760
I know damn well it'd be a pain 
in my ass to keep you here!

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:01.160
The thing is...

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:04.180
To put it another way, 
Hoshin was Banan's sunset!

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:05.640
Oh, really?

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.690
I still don't understand your idioms at all,

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:09.230
but as long as you realize—

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.020
What's with you guys?

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.530
Given your lack of education, 
you might not have understood that.

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:17.060
"Hoshin was Banan's sunset" is a saying

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:19.780
based on the tale of how the 
legendary trader, Hoshin,

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.550
brought the small nation of Banan to ruin.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:26.520
It gives your opponent two options: 
surrender or face an all-out attack.

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:28.540
Surrender or all-out attack?

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:32.090
Garf, are you so dumb that 
you didn't understand me?

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:36.430
You're the one who'd better 
watch what you say, Ram!

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:41.260
Just 'cause I'm hot for ya, that don't
 mean I won't twist yer arm.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.710
Take him back to where he was!

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:46.870
Y-You're really fixated on 
keeping me confined, aren't you?

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.280
Keeping me here is bad news,

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:50.230
so if you can let me go right 
now for free, why wouldn't you?!

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:53.040
I dunno what the hell you are!

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:54.990
That means I can't let you outside!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:59.350
That decision may upset Roswaal-sama.

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.540
Because to Roswaal-sama, Barusu is...

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:05.000
a useless employee. He could
 easily be discarded.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.770
You've got some nerve, saying that right now!

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:09.370
It would upset Roswaal?

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:11.790
How much do you think
he cares about this place,

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:14.130
about the old hag or anyone else?!

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:15.950
He doesn't give a damn!

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:17.720
Not about you either, Ram!

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:18.650
Roswaal-sama is—

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:21.090
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:24.850
I don't give a shit about that bastard!

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:28.640
We're done here! Hand him over!

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:29.520
I'm gonna tie him up and—

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:29.520
Ram-san!

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:30.440
Go!

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:33.150
Damn small fry!

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.810
You can't afford to be distracted, Garf.

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:42.120
Get outta my way!

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:45.420
Hang on, Otto! Why—

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:47.540
You would've been in danger if we'd stayed!

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.610
Ram-san and I made this decision together!

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.760
Wh-What are you doing?

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:56.140
Something I was hoping 
I wouldn't have to resort to.

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:58.380
It would've been better if I hadn't had to!

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:08.180
What are those?

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:12.880
The people of Arlam?

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.420
What did I tell you?

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:16.740
I have some very reliable helpers!

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.190
You weren't just talking about Ram?

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:21.450
Subaru-sama! Please take care!

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:23.450
This way! In here!

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:26.700
Otto-san, take care of Subaru-sama!

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:29.800
Why are they all doing something so crazy?

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:32.460
That's not very convincing, coming from you!

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.740
Keep going straight, 
and you'll find the barrier.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:39.080
What about everyone else?!

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:40.440
We'll stall your pursuers!

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:43.220
We can buy enough time for 
you to escape, no problem!

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:30.920
Gar...fiel...

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:38.270
I-I'll...

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:40.740
do as you say.

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:43.820
So please, don't hurt...

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.540
anyone else...

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:59.410
You complete idiot!

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:15.260
G...

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:19.900
Garfiel!

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:44.130
S-Stay away from Subaru-sama, you monster!

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:45.700
Sto—

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:52.350
Stop it! Please!

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.560
No one needs to die but me!

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:59.450
That's enough! That's enough, Patrasche!

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:22.940
Why... am I here?

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:29.370
It's morning?

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:34.310
Damn it... How long have I been asleep?

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:37.600
Huh?

00:14:51.270 --> 00:14:52.680
What's going on?

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:04.020
I can't! I can't! I can't!

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.140
I have to get them back,

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:10.980
whatever it takes...

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:22.900
There's...

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:24.890
no one here?

00:15:58.270 --> 00:15:59.380
A rabbit?

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:03.280
Why is there a rabbit here?

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:16.530
Why...

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:25.050
Why? Why? Why?

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:26.410
Why?! Why?!

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:28.350
Why?!

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:33.890
You have once again earned the qualification.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:35.680
I invite you...

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:37.200
to a witch's tea party.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:44.020
I don't often invite the same 
guest to my tea parties twice.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:46.200
Feel free to be proud.

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:51.260
I feel so calm, it's kind of creepy.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:53.340
What's going on?

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:56.270
It's because of the tea you drank last time.

00:17:56.270 --> 00:18:01.100
It directly affected your 
Sloth Witch Factor, encouraging stability.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:05.220
If not for that, your soul itself 
would have crumbled to pieces.

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:09.480
Now, I'm ready to accept your gratitude.

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:14.050
Can I assume this will keep working,
 even after I'm back outside?

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:17.400
Well, we <i>are</i> talking about your mental state.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:21.120
So long as you remember what 
happened here, you should be fine.

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.120
So... where's that gratitude?

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:25.170
Echidna...

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:28.290
Is there a way to overwrite the vow?

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:33.680
You know, the one that makes me forget 
about you once I step outside.

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:37.120
So long as it stands, my soul's 
still likely to fall apart.

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:39.060
Well, that's true, but...

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:42.510
Besides, my soul isn't the only problem here.

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:45.640
I want to be able to remember you regardless.

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:46.640
Huh?

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:50.810
If it comes at a price, 
I'll pay whatever you want.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:55.310
In return, don't hide yourself in my memories.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:57.760
A-All right...

00:18:58.680 --> 00:18:59.230
Huh?

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:02.850
Really?! Thanks a lot!

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:04.760
And no changing your mind, all right?!

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:07.600
I wouldn't do something so shameless.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:12.540
I wouldn't, but I think 
you're being a bit unfair.

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:19.260
And then you gulp down my 
bodily fluids like that...

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:21.760
I forgot about that!

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:24.130
So? Where's that gratitude?

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:26.720
I don't believe I've heard it yet.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:30.800
Yeah, thanks for making me 
this nasty tea, you witch!

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:33.740
That kind of gratitude
wounds my maidenly heart.

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:44.320
What? You have something else to say?

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:46.750
Quit playing around.

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:50.060
Just how much do you know about me?

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:53.320
If you're asking what I know, 
I know only what I know.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:54.710
If you're asking what I want to know,

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.420
I want to know everything in this world.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:02.130
There's no way it shouldn't 
seem strange to you.

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:07.900
For you, this is happening right after 
your last tea party with me, isn't it?

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:10.600
So if you don't find this strange,

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:12.310
then...

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:13.560
Then?

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:20.620
Then... that can only mean 
you know how this happened.

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:29.700
Then test me.

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:38.620
Y-You might not even have 
time to regret saying that!

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:43.580
If that proves to be true, can I 
expect you to break down crying

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:44.900
over my corpse?

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.270
Echidna...

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:55.200
I..

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:00.220
I've been Returning by Death!

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:13.000
Hmm...

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:16.670
It's a bit embarrassing to have 
you staring at me like that.

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:22.160
Wh-When I... When I die, I go back in time

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:23.930
and restart the world.

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:26.220
I Return by Death.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:27.780
I heard you.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:31.260
And before I heard you, I saw you.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.780
I... Return by Death!

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.640
Return by Death! Return by Death!

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:38.120
Return by Death! Return by Death!

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:39.830
Hey, calm down! I know how you feel but—

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:42.410
I've been Returning by Death!

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.960
I've died and started again over and over!

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:46.990
I Return by Death!

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:49.440
I get it, I said! Just listen to m—

00:21:49.440 --> 00:21:50.620
I've been...

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:54.830
Returning by Death...

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:58.760
to start again... over and over...

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:05.720
I...

00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:09.010
All this time...

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:13.140
Ever since I came to this world...

00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:17.640
I've never, ever been able 
to say it to anyone...

00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:22.540
Over and over... all alone... 
alone this whole time...

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:25.860
I... I...

00:22:37.480 --> 00:22:38.740
I know.

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:39.830
<b>I know</b>

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:48.750
I know every step you've 
taken on your path here.

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:52.330
I was watching.

00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:59.020
But watching is all I was doing.

00:23:01.020 --> 00:23:05.620
So if you can, I'd like 
you to tell me yourself...

00:23:06.630 --> 00:23:10.970
what you have thought, how you have felt,

00:23:10.970 --> 00:23:12.900
and how much weight you have carried.

00:23:14.320 --> 00:23:15.960
I want to know.

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:22.230
After all, I'm the Witch of Greed, 
who wants to know everything in this world.

00:23:23.680 --> 00:23:25.500
That's me... Echidna.

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:29.590
<b>The Value of Life</b>
